<title>USA: Koch lowers most U.S. posted crude 75 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Koch lowers most U.S. posted crude 75 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil Co said it had lowered the price it will pay for most grades of U.S. crude oil by 75 cents, effective Monday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.75 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.00 a barrel. Oklahoma sweet is down to $18.75.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is lowered $1.25 to $18.25.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
